From: Kiwibot JP5 bring-up <pedro@kiwibot.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Sep 2026 13:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] misc: bluedroid_pm: do not kfree the embedded wakeup source on remove

struct bluedroid_pm_data embeds `struct wakeup_source wake_lock` and initialises it with
wakeup_source_init()/wakeup_source_add(). On kernels >= 5.9 the remove path calls
wakeup_source_destroy(), which kfree()s the wakeup source: an invalid free 64 bytes inside
the kmalloc-512 private data (KASAN: double-free or invalid-free in kfree, bluedroid_pm_remove
-> wakeup_source_destroy). The robot startup runs `modprobe -r bluedroid_pm`, so this
corrupted the heap on every boot. Undo the wakeup_source_add() instead; the memory is freed
with the private data by kfree(bluedroid_pm) below.
---
 nvidia/drivers/misc/bluedroid_pm.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/nvidia/drivers/misc/bluedroid_pm.c
+++ b/nvidia/drivers/misc/bluedroid_pm.c
@@ -462,7 +462,8 @@
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 9, 0)
 		wakeup_source_trash(&bluedroid_pm->wake_lock);
 #else
-		wakeup_source_destroy(&bluedroid_pm->wake_lock);
+		/* wake_lock is embedded: never kfree() it (wakeup_source_destroy would) */
+		wakeup_source_remove(&bluedroid_pm->wake_lock);
 #endif
 		gpio_free(bluedroid_pm->ext_wake);
 		remove_bt_proc_interface();
